// What Gradle says to the shared scope rules: names are bare tokens, so every name that is not a
// declaration is a use, and the rows list the declarations: an import, and a `def`/`var` name with a value (the parser
// splits a typed declaration, so only that form is sure). The reads inside a GString: `${...}` (`interpolated`), `$name`
// (`expansions`). Format: core_semantics::scopes::rows.
names Ident
bare
interpolated String "${"

ImportDeclaration inert declares=value|type|import token=last/?has-token.".*":skip:declare
LocalVariableDeclaration declares=value|let
VariableDeclarator token=first/?has-token."=":declare:skip
